      "title": "All 14 Korean consonants in one song! 가 나 다 라 마 바 사 아 자 차 카 타 파 하 #learnkorean",
      "text": "Sing along with Mongle — one song, all 14 basic Korean consonants (Hangul).\n\nEvery line builds a syllable: consonant + ㅏ (a)\nㄱ + ㅏ = 가 (ga) · ㄴ + ㅏ = 나 (na) · ㄷ + ㅏ = 다 (da) · ㄹ + ㅏ = 라 (ra) …\nㅇ is silent at the start, so ㅇ + ㅏ = 아 (a) — shh!\nConsonants are coral, vowels are blue — watch them join into one syllable.\n\n\"그 더하기 아는?\" (g + a = ?) — say the answer before the song does!\nRomanization appears under every letter, and English captions (CC) have the lyrics.\nAt the end, try reading 나무 · 바다 · 모자 (tree · sea · hat).\n\nHangul for Beginners · 한글 초보단계 #2 — after the vowel song (#1).\nSYNK LAB · learn Korean the fun way, with Mongle.\n#learnkorean #hangul #koreanalphabet",
      "alt": [
        "A felt kid and the coral felt mascot Mongle build Korean syllables (ㄱ + ㅏ = 가), consonant in coral and vowel in blue, under a white card reading “All 14 Korean consonants in one song!”"
      ],
